  "ref": "ACT.18.10",
  "review_notes": [
    "λαός ἐστί μοι πολύς → 'I have much people': the copula takes 'have' and the possessive dative takes the English subject 'I'. Reading 'I have' as one unit on the copula remains defensible, but rule 2 keeps the dative's own English on the dative.",
    "ἐπιθήσεταί σοι splits under rule 106: the ASV writes a verb word ('set') for the compound, so 'on' realizes the dative government and rides with σοι."
  ]
